  "reasoning": "The patient reports a \"silver like dusting\" on the skin and peeling skin on the arms and back. This specific description of silvery scales or dusting is a hallmark clinical feature of psoriasis. While drug reaction and fungal infection can sometimes involve peeling or rashes, they lack the characteristic silver appearance; drug reaction references typically include systemic signs like tremors, and fungal infection references describe red, itchy rashes or bumps. Allergy typically presents with swelling, sneezing, or hives rather than silvery peeling skin. Thus, the facts firmly establish psoriasis as the single correct diagnosis.",
  "final_answer": "[DIAGNOSIS]psoriasis[/DIAGNOSIS]"
